# Line endings: LF in the repository *and* in the working tree.
#
# `eol=lf` is the part that matters. The repository was already all-LF, but a Windows
# clone with `core.autocrlf=true` (the installer's default) rewrites files to CRLF on
# checkout — and then biome reports every one of them as misformatted while `git diff`
# shows nothing at all, because the index was LF the whole time. Formatting was
# therefore not reproducible across machines, and `--write` produced changes that
# could not be committed and came back on the next checkout.
#
# Pinning it here overrides whatever each developer has configured locally, which is
# the only way this stays fixed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Assets Git must never touch. Content detection already catches these; declaring them
# means a corrupted font or screenshot can never be blamed on eol conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
